# DDD Architecture & Boundaries

## Layers (one folder per bounded context)

```
src/<module>/
  domain/          ← pure TS — zero @nestjs/*, Prisma, HTTP
  application/     ← CQRS orchestration — no Prisma, no HTTP types
  infrastructure/  ← Prisma, HTTP clients, messaging, cache adapters
  presentation/    ← controllers, guards — HTTP edge only
```

**Dependency direction:** Presentation → Application → Domain. Infrastructure → Domain.
Application may inject Infrastructure **via interface tokens only** (same module).
Domain never imports Application, Infrastructure, or Presentation.

## New feature checklist

- Aggregate extends `AggregateRoot<T>`, `#` private fields, static `create(...)`
- Mutating methods: guard → mutate → `touch()` → `addDomainEvent(...)`
- Invariants throw typed errors extending `BusinessError`
- Child entities extend `BaseDomain<T>` — no repository, no events
- Value objects immutable, equality by value; repos/ports are interfaces only
- Handlers inject via token; Prisma **standard CRUD** repos **must** extend `PrismaCrudRepositoryBase` (never reimplement `findById` / `findAll` / `findPaged` / `create` / `update` / `delete` / `count` by hand)
- Prisma constructor: `BasePrismaService<PrismaClient>` + `super(database, '<generatedDelegateKey>')`; use `this.delegate` / `this.client` — never an untyped proxy or stale model names

## Cross-module access

| Operation | Use | Never |
|-----------|-----|--------|
| **Read** | Provider **read-only port** or Facade query | Foreign repo / command / query |
| **Write** | Owning context **Facade** → bus → handler | Repo, write port, foreign command |

- Module imports must stay a **DAG** (no cycles).
- Repository tokens from packages are for **host persistence wiring only**.
- Workflow: external callers use `WorkflowFacade` only.
- Correspondence: `CorrespondenceRequestEvent` or exported commands/queries — never its repos.

## User identity

| Field | Who may use |
|-------|-------------|
| `idpSub` | Auth guards/adapters/token-vault only |
| `userId` | All domain modules (audit, access control) |

- Reads anywhere → `IUserLookupPort`. Writes in apps → `UserFacade`. Packages never inject `UserFacade`.
- Never pass raw `idpSub` to non-auth modules. Audit: `caller.userId ?? caller.idpSub`.

## Post-implementation (mandatory)

```powershell
npx tsc --noEmit
npm run build
npm test
```

If Prisma models changed: `npm run generate:db` first. Task is done only when all three exit `0`.
